WEBVTT

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.150
I had a dream about my childhood.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.640
I forgot about it.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.250
And I was never able to recall it.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:50.030
A dream about the distant past.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:05.420
<b>Kara no Kyoukai</b>

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:20.030
I, Azaka Kokutou, am a 16-year-old magus apprentice.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:23.070
I have a brother named Mikiya Kokutou,

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.440
a master named Touko Aozaki,

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.070
and a rival in love named Shiki Ryougi.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:35.550
I'm what you would call a troubled young lady.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:39.450
I'm going to explain myself so there won't be any misunderstandings.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:44.170
I'm not troubled by the fact that I love my own brother.

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:50.510
I seriously love Mikiya Kokutou to the point where I can't believe it myself.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.890
I got adopted by my uncle,

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.890
entered a boarding school called Reien,

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:04.690
and lived away from Mikiya so that he would forget about me being his younger sister.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:09.690
So there's only one problem I'm facing right now.

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:15.200
It's that woman who came barging in and took my prize!

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:22.070
Mikiya, I'm home!

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:27.010
Welcome home, Azaka.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.230
Hey.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.860
Oh yeah. This is the first time you've met her, huh?

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:34.840
Let me introduce her.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.700
She's my classmate, Shiki Ryougi.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.970
I need to get that woman to break up with Mikiya as fast as possible

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:43.100
and get him away from dangerous things.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:50.030
I even became an apprentice magus so that I could match her mentally and physically

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.730
and become her rival.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:57.670
This is a story about such an admirable girl: Me.

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:00.200
But...

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.040
What's the meaning of this, Touko?

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:10.380
Oh, sounds like the secret weapon has arrived.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.010
How is that a secret weapon?

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:16.310
Do you remember my request?

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:20.080
Detection and elimination of the magus who is using fairies

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.520
to spread anxiety among the students at Reien Academy.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:30.270
That's right. Since you can't see the fairies, you'll need the eyes.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.010
T-That's...

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:44.000
I'm Shiki Ryougi, and I came here because I was ordered to by Ms. Touko Aozaki.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:50.170
Stupid Touko!

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:56.380
I can already tell there'll be problems.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.130
Nothing's going to happen.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:03.410
After all, Shiki thinks of Azaka as her little sister.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.040
You don't understand, do you?

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:08.440
Don't understand what?

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.570
Everything.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:20.530
So I've been thinking.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.990
Touko may actually be stupid.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:32.030
You're right. It's crazy to have you of all people sneak into the academy.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:37.010
This sucks. I'm definitely the victim this time.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:41.410
I have to help find fairies on New Years.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.850
I'm sorry.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:49.840
Unfortunately, I don't have this thing called mystic eyes like you or Touko.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.950
Hey, is this your dog?

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.290
He followed us to your room.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:00.620
No.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:06.370
He's the dog of my roommate, Seo, who happens to be traveling overseas with her family.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:11.550
She asked me to take care of him,

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:15.550
but it's so annoying because he misbehaves like his master.

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:21.550
I see.

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:27.030
This place tolerates pets even though it's a strict school, huh?

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:32.980
It's not like they tolerate them!

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:35.060
Why did you bring him here?

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:37.610
Why? He's been with us for a while.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:40.950
Hurry up and take him back to the room.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.800
Hurry up!

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:58.420
We're a boarding school,

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:01.410
so there are many students at school even during winter break.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.140
Please try not to do anything that stands out-

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:10.210
That's the chapel. Did you see something?

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:11.890
Do they hold Mass there?

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:16.960
Like, "Our Father called to heaven"?

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:18.530
What are you going to do by calling him there?

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:21.660
Oh, is it "Our Father in heaven"?

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:28.410
First of all,

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:32.240
we'll hear from the teacher of class 1-4.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:34.650
That Hayama guy?

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:39.140
No. Mr. Hayama suddenly disappeared in November.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:42.850
There was a rumor about him being associated with dangerous people,

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.430
so he may be deep in Tokyo Bay by now.

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:46.420
fish without permission
Please don't feed the

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:49.630
How did a guy like that manage to become a teacher here?
fish without permission
Please don't feed the

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:51.890
He's the chairman's younger brother.
fish without permission
Please don't feed the

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:53.590
fish without permission
Please don't feed the

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:56.440
So who's the teacher now?
fish without permission
Please don't feed the

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:58.350
<b>I'm in</b>

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.360
It's Mr. Kurogiri.
<b>I'm in</b>

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.370
I'm Azaka Kokutou from class 1-1.

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:11.920
Did you receive the message from Mother?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:14.330
Yes.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:24.020
The rumor about fairies who steal memories?

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:30.010
Yes, there have been a few times when the students asked me about them.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:33.440
And what did you do?

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:39.720
I told them that they shouldn't worry about it too much since the fairies are just mischievous.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:41.260
Do you believe in them?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:42.530
Yes.

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:50.650
Legends about fairies may be rare in Japan, but they're popular in Europe.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:55.720
You're from Wales, was it?

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:56.120
Yes.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:04.050
There are many stories in my country about cute fairies such as cat fairies and dog fairies.

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:07.180
I'm rather fond of them too.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:19.840
Have you ever heard of fairies killing people?

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:27.730
Are you talking about what happened to Kaori Tachibana?

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:28.850
Yes.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:30.700
A student from class 1-4 said

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:33.870
that Kaori was attacked by fairies and that she didn't commit suicide-

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:35.910
Excuse me.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:41.080
Oh, Ouji.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:43.000
Is it time already?

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.690
Yes, Mr. Satsuki.

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:48.510
It's already past the appointed time of one o'clock.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:49.910
Time isn't eternal, so please use it efficiently.

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:52.750
She's Misaya Ouji. She's the student council president.
Time isn't eternal, so please use it efficiently.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:54.020
And the chairman's daughter.
Time isn't eternal, so please use it efficiently.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:56.880
You're so strict, Ouji.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:00.770
You're bringing up a difficult subject like eternity.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:10.940
I don't think what happened to Tachibana was the fairies' doing.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.400
Kokutou, was it?

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:16.980
Yes, Ouji.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:21.160
Mr. Satsuki has nothing to do with that.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.840
Please try not to trouble him too much about it.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:26.460
Okay.

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:55.830
We can't talk to class 1-4, the people who were involved.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.380
Nobody wants to talk about it.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:00.080
I guess we should talk to others.

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:03.880
What's wrong, Shiki?

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:13.700
Oh, you were surprised because Mr. Kurogiri looks like Mikiya, right?

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:17.850
Yeah. So that's why you act modest in front of him, huh?

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:21.170
W-What's that supposed to mean?

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:22.950
It sounds like you're suggesting something.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:25.730
No. It's just something that came to my mind.

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:27.630
A-Anyway.

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:30.620
He's a person named Satsuki Kurogiri.

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:34.530
No matter how much he may look like him, he's not Mikiya Kokutou.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:38.240
Look like him? It's more like...

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:40.830
More like?

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.250
Shiki?

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.730
What's wrong, Shiki?

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:08.930
It's time for work.

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:13.650
Hey, Shiki. Don't be so selfish.

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.260
Hey, Shiki!

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:17.820
Geez!

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:41.880
Azaka Kokutou.

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:42.590
Eh?

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.850
Hey, Azaka. You're gonna catch a cold.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.530
M-Mikiya...

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:38.430
Punch!

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:41.540
Ow!

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:44.050
What are you doing all of a sudden, you idiot!

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:45.520
That should wake you up.

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:46.410
Yeah.

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:50.800
Azaka. Do you know what time it is?

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:54.650
It's just past two in the afternoon.

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:04.770
Shiki, could it be...?

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:07.240
The fairy took it away.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:20.100
I don't know who this magus is, but I'm gonna beat him silly.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:24.210
I won't forgive him even if he apologizes or cries!

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:34.350
This isn't it either.

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:37.010
What?

00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:40.240
You're pretty bold, Azaka.

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:45.860
The chairman's at some New Year's party and won't be back until tomorrow, so...

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:50.240
This is the only one that's locked.

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:53.940
Shiki?

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:16.460
Damn, girl...

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:23.620
Thank you, God!

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:30.810
<b>For departmental use only:  '98
Class 1-4 Kaori Tachibana Investigation Notes</b>

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:39.940
It's here.

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:45.500
It's the internal record of the questioning conducted on the students of class 1-4

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:47.290
right after that thing with Kaori Tachibana.

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:55.540
"Kaori Tachibana started to act strange at the beginning of the second quarter."

00:17:56.040 --> 00:18:01.810
"She suddenly grew thin, looked pale, and she always seemed afraid of something."

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.930
And on the day of the incident, she said during class...

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:05.790
Help!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:08.290
The fairies...

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:11.010
The fairies are coming!

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:15.330
Tachibana!

00:18:15.810 --> 00:18:17.400
Wait! Tachibana!

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:22.730
And the old school building caught on fire after that.

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:27.770
They made such a coherent testimony, but now they don't even remember it?

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:32.950
The magus using the fairies is trying to erase what happened to Kaori Tachibana.

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:35.420
Hayama's the suspicious one.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:36.170
<b>Hideo Hayama</b>

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:38.340
He looks pale.
<b>Hideo Hayama</b>

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:42.570
This is...

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.220
Touko!

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:24.360
So, did you see anyone suspicious out of the people you met today?

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:28.920
I see.

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:31.260
Hey, Azaka.

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:36.240
Would the memories taken by the fairies never return?

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:39.710
I think so. But why're you bringing it up now?

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:40.840
No reason.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:44.090
People don't die from getting their memory taken away.

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:45.280
I'm a good example.

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:50.910
Are you saying that murder isn't the fairy user's intention?

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:54.990
I think it's just turning out that way.

00:19:55.780 --> 00:20:00.540
First of all, it's easy to kill someone without relying on fairies.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.360
That's true.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:06.380
I see, taking memories away means...

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:11.890
There's something someone wants to hide and wants people to forget.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:25.640
Shiki. You have something you're hiding, right?

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:32.830
Don't play dumb.

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:36.330
I'm telling you to take out the knife you just stole from the dining hall.

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:40.400
It's just a knife. Don't worry about it.

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:44.380
No. You're someone who can kill a lock with a ruler.

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:46.870
I'm collecting them to look at them.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:49.670
You're not going to take it out no matter what, huh?

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:51.840
You're persistent.

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:55.100
All right. I'm going to resort to force.

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:59.220
Give it to me!

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:04.310
I said give it to me, you...

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:07.440
Got it!

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:10.740
You're ridiculously strong!

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:13.470
Excuse me.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:17.200
But that should be enough to push Mikiya down.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.490
What did you just say?!

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:26.250
I didn't mean anything else. I just thought so.

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:33.030
You can tell?

00:21:33.030 --> 00:21:34.530
I dunno.

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:40.620
I'm not the one who noticed. At the very least, I'm sure he doesn't know.

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:41.520
Isn't that good enough?

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:43.260
I see...

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:52.640
What's so good about him?

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:56.480
You two are siblings, right?

00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:01.620
I have a confession.

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:05.180
I like special things.

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:09.920
More accurately, it seems I'm attracted to taboo things.

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:15.440
So I think it's actually a fortunate thing that the person I love is a close relative of mine.

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:18.210
You pervert.

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:21.910
Don't call me that, weirdo.

00:22:27.440 --> 00:22:34.220
The problem is that I don't remember when I fell in love with him.

00:22:35.800 --> 00:22:37.970
Shiki. Wake up.

00:22:37.970 --> 00:22:39.700
Geez, wake up.

00:22:39.700 --> 00:22:44.000
I said we're going to check out the arson site in the old school building first thing in the morning.

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:46.520
Wake up, stupid Shiki!

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:49.700
Keep sleeping forever!

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:02.190
Are you here, Kokutou?

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:04.390
Your brother called you.

00:23:05.090 --> 00:23:06.280
Brother?

00:23:20.220 --> 00:23:24.250
Okay Azaka, pull yourself together and start the investigation.

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:33.400
Last year in November,

00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:38.280
Kaori Tachibana screamed that the fairies are coming, ran out of the classroom,

00:23:38.280 --> 00:23:41.130
and ran into this old school building.

00:23:41.130 --> 00:23:46.120
And she set this spot on fire to kill herself.

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:51.690
The fairy user is taking this memory away from the students.

00:23:52.810 --> 00:23:56.030
What's the magus's goal?

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:09.700
Good morning, Kokutou.

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:13.030
Good morning, Ouji.

00:24:13.030 --> 00:24:15.550
What an unusual place to meet.

00:24:16.130 --> 00:24:19.800
Would you like to join me for morning service?

00:24:22.130 --> 00:24:22.970
Sure.

00:24:23.750 --> 00:24:25.520
If you don't mind.

00:24:33.680 --> 00:24:35.430
Thank you, Kokutou.

00:24:36.650 --> 00:24:40.450
It's been a while since I prayed with someone.

00:24:41.240 --> 00:24:45.620
If <i>that</i> had never happened, she would still be standing next to me.

00:24:47.130 --> 00:24:49.180
Are you talking about Kaori Tachibana?

00:24:49.180 --> 00:24:49.970
Yes.

00:24:50.880 --> 00:24:54.930
She was like a little sister to me.

00:24:54.930 --> 00:24:58.970
She was clumsy and would always get the short end of the stick,

00:24:59.830 --> 00:25:02.890
but she was kind and more religious than anyone.

00:25:04.580 --> 00:25:05.540
But...

00:25:16.150 --> 00:25:19.720
I want to erase all traces of her disgrace.

00:25:21.430 --> 00:25:22.990
It's you, huh?

00:25:24.490 --> 00:25:25.950
I obtained magic

00:25:27.140 --> 00:25:29.440
for Kaori's sake.

00:25:34.480 --> 00:25:36.770
Please back out of this, Kokutou.

00:25:36.770 --> 00:25:39.490
I don't want to fight you.

00:25:39.490 --> 00:25:42.230
You're the one who made the first move.

00:25:43.480 --> 00:25:46.320
Yes. That's why I know.

00:25:46.320 --> 00:25:51.980
You love your real brother from the bottom of your heart, even though you don't remember why.

00:25:55.530 --> 00:25:57.900
You're very good.

00:25:59.050 --> 00:26:01.030
So you know everything, huh?

00:26:06.130 --> 00:26:08.170
Then I'll come out with it.

00:26:08.170 --> 00:26:12.920
I don't have the exact memory of when I fell in love with him.

00:26:13.580 --> 00:26:15.570
Before I knew it, I was in love with him.

00:26:17.730 --> 00:26:23.800
So if you can draw out that memory, I'll let you go.

00:26:27.990 --> 00:26:29.680
That's impossible.

00:26:29.680 --> 00:26:33.730
The fairies can only take away memories you remember.

00:26:33.730 --> 00:26:38.440
No one can recover lost memories, the oblivion.

00:26:40.200 --> 00:26:43.930
And Kokutou. You said you'd let me go,

00:26:44.280 --> 00:26:49.200
but I have no intention of stopping after merely taking away their memories.

00:26:49.440 --> 00:26:50.910
Ouji...?

00:26:50.910 --> 00:26:53.460
They deserve to be punished.

00:27:01.760 --> 00:27:07.850
Kaori was dragged into it, but nobody tried to help her.

00:27:07.850 --> 00:27:11.880
They didn't do anything. That itself is a crime.

00:27:14.050 --> 00:27:15.890
What happened, Ouji?

00:27:20.110 --> 00:27:24.140
You... You pushed her to commit suicide!

00:27:24.140 --> 00:27:27.620
Stop! Don't come near me!

00:27:36.450 --> 00:27:38.010
What is this?

00:27:38.010 --> 00:27:40.030
You know, right, Kokutou?

00:27:40.950 --> 00:27:44.870
You need something to make familiars out of.

00:27:45.200 --> 00:27:46.560
It was an accident.

00:27:59.610 --> 00:28:01.440
Then Hayama is...

00:28:07.740 --> 00:28:09.940
Go to sleep, Kokutou.

00:28:10.270 --> 00:28:14.990
I shall repeat your grief within your hollow sleep.

00:28:18.510 --> 00:28:19.420
Kokutou.

00:28:20.240 --> 00:28:21.450
Kokutou.

00:28:22.190 --> 00:28:23.270
Azaka.

00:28:23.970 --> 00:28:25.210
Kokutou.

00:28:26.310 --> 00:28:28.510
M-Mikiya.

00:28:28.510 --> 00:28:29.050
What?

00:28:29.600 --> 00:28:32.630
M-Mr. Kurogiri. I'm sorry.

00:28:33.080 --> 00:28:35.340
You don't look well.

00:28:35.340 --> 00:28:36.810
Did something happen?

00:28:38.240 --> 00:28:39.810
Well...

00:28:41.420 --> 00:28:43.830
Wait, I remember.

00:28:43.830 --> 00:28:45.340
But why?

00:28:54.850 --> 00:28:57.730
The students of class 4 disappeared?

00:28:57.730 --> 00:29:00.270
Is there a secret Mass or something?

00:29:00.270 --> 00:29:01.920
That can't be...

00:29:02.890 --> 00:29:03.940
Could it be?!

00:29:05.160 --> 00:29:06.340
Mr. Kurogiri.

00:29:06.670 --> 00:29:09.700
Did you see where Ouji went?

00:29:10.240 --> 00:29:13.970
No. I haven't seen anyone besides you, Kokutou.

00:29:15.590 --> 00:29:19.130
So she's resorting to force right after her persuasion fails?

00:29:19.130 --> 00:29:20.550
Resorting to force?

00:29:20.550 --> 00:29:27.320
Yes. Misaya Ouji intends to erase the memory about Kaori Tachibana from all the students in class 1-4.

00:29:30.370 --> 00:29:32.900
Shiki, let's split up and search for them.

00:29:32.900 --> 00:29:35.470
Can you go search the school building again?

00:29:35.470 --> 00:29:37.120
I'll search the forest.

00:29:37.120 --> 00:29:38.490
I have an idea.

00:29:38.730 --> 00:29:42.330
Oh, there's nothing over there.

00:30:02.640 --> 00:30:03.880
Never mind.

00:30:03.880 --> 00:30:05.110
Please be careful.

00:30:05.390 --> 00:30:07.640
Okay. Excuse us.

00:30:41.180 --> 00:30:42.540
No way...

00:31:18.410 --> 00:31:20.830
Where did she go?

00:31:21.500 --> 00:31:25.260
I'm sure she's in this school.

00:31:26.700 --> 00:31:28.640
And that classroom...

00:31:39.440 --> 00:31:40.870
Mikiya...

00:31:42.620 --> 00:31:46.650
What would Mikiya do?

00:31:47.250 --> 00:31:49.360
What if it's Mikiya...?

00:32:10.580 --> 00:32:12.650
Why won't you cry?

00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:15.310
I don't know.

00:32:21.270 --> 00:32:24.080
Hey, why won't you cry?

00:32:40.640 --> 00:32:44.880
Geez, I'm tired. What're you doing?

00:32:49.660 --> 00:32:51.080
Oh, Shiki.

00:32:51.080 --> 00:32:52.440
Did you find something?

00:32:53.490 --> 00:32:54.530
No.

00:32:54.530 --> 00:32:56.690
Anyway, you got a call.

00:32:58.530 --> 00:33:00.550
It's from your brother.

00:33:06.030 --> 00:33:08.540
Information about Hideo Hayama?

00:33:09.170 --> 00:33:14.300
Shiki requested it, but it's more suitable that I report it to you.

00:33:14.630 --> 00:33:18.640
Oh, Shiki requested that?

00:33:18.640 --> 00:33:22.300
Shiki said that you're concerned about Hayama.

00:33:22.620 --> 00:33:25.990
Yes. But I never said I wanted him investigated.

00:33:25.990 --> 00:33:30.750
I don't want you associated with dangerous things like this.

00:33:30.750 --> 00:33:35.050
I'm sure Shiki isn't worried about your well-being.

00:33:36.530 --> 00:33:37.820
Nothing I can do about that.

00:33:38.320 --> 00:33:41.780
Right now, Shiki's worried about <i>your</i> well-being.

00:33:47.170 --> 00:33:49.350
So, what did you find?

00:33:49.680 --> 00:33:53.230
Okay, I'll tell you about Shiki's request first.

00:33:53.230 --> 00:33:55.520
And I'll give you Touko's message as well.

00:33:56.740 --> 00:33:58.180
From Touko?

00:34:09.690 --> 00:34:12.300
I told her just like you told me.

00:34:12.300 --> 00:34:14.240
Okay, thanks.

00:34:15.110 --> 00:34:17.700
You're really not going to go help them?

00:34:17.700 --> 00:34:22.100
Satsuki Kurogiri is a dangerous magus called God's Word, right?

00:34:22.440 --> 00:34:24.700
I'm sure it won't get serious.

00:34:25.350 --> 00:34:30.920
He controls people's recognition using words, but he has no other ways to attack.

00:34:31.400 --> 00:34:33.300
I told her a counter-measure.

00:34:33.300 --> 00:34:36.590
And if she's my apprentice, she should manage.

00:34:37.300 --> 00:34:39.600
Enough of that. Let's eat.

00:35:00.180 --> 00:35:01.030
Kokutou.

00:35:01.710 --> 00:35:04.300
Good evening, Mr. Kurogiri.

00:35:05.920 --> 00:35:07.260
There's nothing over there.

00:35:07.260 --> 00:35:08.220
I'm in a hurry, so please excuse me.
There's nothing over there.

00:35:08.220 --> 00:35:09.460
I'm in a hurry, so please excuse me.

00:36:13.490 --> 00:36:19.190
Isn't it going a bit too far to make a whole class burn to death like Kaori?

00:36:20.790 --> 00:36:23.820
Don't they deserve it, Kokutou?

00:36:24.300 --> 00:36:26.820
This will all end tonight.

00:36:29.930 --> 00:36:33.070
The real culprit won't get in my way either.

00:36:37.820 --> 00:36:41.490
You use a circuitous approach, huh?

00:36:41.490 --> 00:36:42.860
What're you after?

00:36:42.860 --> 00:36:43.940
I don't know.

00:36:43.940 --> 00:36:47.500
I merely granted someone else's wish.

00:36:47.500 --> 00:36:51.300
This is happening because of their wish.

00:36:51.810 --> 00:36:54.680
I personally don't have a goal.

00:36:55.180 --> 00:36:56.840
This must be fate.

00:36:57.200 --> 00:37:02.120
I came to this country because Souren Araya requested that I return

00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:06.260
the memory that you lost in oblivion two years ago.

00:37:06.980 --> 00:37:11.120
No, you're also looking for your lost memory.

00:37:11.650 --> 00:37:15.770
I can see your mind hidden behind your words.

00:37:16.730 --> 00:37:19.210
That's my only role.

00:37:20.400 --> 00:37:22.090
As for Ouji...

00:37:22.420 --> 00:37:28.130
Well, in human terms, I'm just killing time.

00:37:28.870 --> 00:37:31.720
One needs amusement to live.

00:37:31.720 --> 00:37:35.510
Just living would make you a machine.

00:37:35.980 --> 00:37:38.270
Are you a magus too?

00:37:39.330 --> 00:37:40.220
Yes.

00:37:40.220 --> 00:37:43.220
I'm a magus who controls words.

00:37:43.220 --> 00:37:45.650
I'm called God's Word.

00:37:48.560 --> 00:37:50.670
Let's stop playing with fire,

00:37:52.430 --> 00:37:53.410
Ouji.

00:37:55.090 --> 00:37:58.160
Please don't joke around, Kokutou.

00:37:58.610 --> 00:38:00.740
If you stop now, it'll remain a joke.

00:38:02.280 --> 00:38:05.130
People have died already.

00:38:05.600 --> 00:38:08.000
Yes. Hayama is dead.

00:38:08.380 --> 00:38:11.520
But you didn't kill him.

00:38:11.520 --> 00:38:13.390
The one who killed Hayama is...

00:38:14.600 --> 00:38:16.310
Hayama himself.

00:38:19.130 --> 00:38:22.300
The fairy was the one who told me about it.

00:38:22.790 --> 00:38:28.320
For Kaori's sake, you obtained magic and used Hayama as your magic's foundation.

00:38:28.720 --> 00:38:33.780
But why did the two of them see the illusion of these fairies?

00:38:33.780 --> 00:38:35.150
Illusion?

00:38:35.150 --> 00:38:39.430
Drastically losing weight, becoming emotionally unstable and seeing illusions.

00:38:40.140 --> 00:38:45.330
These are all withdrawal symptoms of a drug addict.

00:38:45.910 --> 00:38:50.770
Kaori tried to commit suicide because she couldn't forgive herself for becoming a drug addict.

00:38:50.770 --> 00:38:56.350
And while Hayama was talking with you, he had a heart attack due to the drug.

00:38:56.780 --> 00:39:03.120
Meaning nobody died and nobody killed anyone, except for Hideo Hayama who killed himself.

00:39:04.060 --> 00:39:09.530
Which just leaves the ones who couldn't save Kaori Tachibana when she was in distress.

00:39:10.230 --> 00:39:13.970
And the one who wanted to look away from that inconvenience is...

00:39:17.510 --> 00:39:20.490
That's why your memory was stolen before anyone's.

00:39:20.490 --> 00:39:22.500
That's why that memory was lost into oblivion.

00:39:22.500 --> 00:39:26.830
You should know already that your revenge is...

00:39:29.600 --> 00:39:33.730
Just a convenient fantasy that you wished for!

00:39:44.710 --> 00:39:47.730
That's good, very good,

00:39:48.130 --> 00:39:49.110
Kokutou!

00:40:11.580 --> 00:40:12.760
AzoLto!

00:40:25.350 --> 00:40:27.900
You're the one fantasizing, Kokutou.

00:40:28.440 --> 00:40:32.700
I used the fairies to eavesdrop on the students in class 4.

00:40:32.700 --> 00:40:35.180
It's the unmistakable truth!

00:40:37.480 --> 00:40:38.840
I see.

00:40:39.650 --> 00:40:40.410
But.

00:40:41.800 --> 00:40:44.120
You couldn't hear from Kaori or Hayama.

00:40:46.360 --> 00:40:52.220
Your truth is a mere rumor born amongst the students after the incident.

00:40:52.960 --> 00:40:55.130
Everything about you came afterwards.

00:40:55.650 --> 00:40:58.300
The motive for your revenge and your magic.

00:41:00.710 --> 00:41:04.870
And the one who gave you your power is...

00:41:21.410 --> 00:41:23.490
You'll lose sight of me.

00:41:26.630 --> 00:41:27.870
Again?!

00:41:31.070 --> 00:41:32.590
That's scary.

00:41:32.590 --> 00:41:35.040
We can't talk if you're trying to kill me.

00:41:35.740 --> 00:41:38.950
But a wish returns to its owner.

00:41:39.290 --> 00:41:43.950
It consumes the host when the host recalls it.

00:41:44.540 --> 00:41:47.070
Your oblivion is of that nature.

00:41:50.150 --> 00:41:51.940
You cannot see here.

00:41:59.280 --> 00:42:01.930
I shall play back the grief.

00:42:01.930 --> 00:42:07.500
Even if you forgot it, the memory is actually recorded inside of you.

00:42:20.990 --> 00:42:22.370
How ridiculous.

00:42:35.760 --> 00:42:36.970
Ouji!

00:42:53.270 --> 00:42:54.000
Outta my way!

00:43:41.060 --> 00:43:42.760
Give it up already!

00:44:12.770 --> 00:44:13.800
Azaka.

00:44:14.830 --> 00:44:16.360
You're late.

00:44:16.360 --> 00:44:17.940
What were you doing?

00:44:21.050 --> 00:44:22.440
Is it over?

00:44:25.350 --> 00:44:26.680
Of course.

00:44:42.560 --> 00:44:43.680
Ciao!

00:44:44.320 --> 00:44:46.950
How are you, Akira?

00:44:52.300 --> 00:44:53.200
Come on.

00:44:57.230 --> 00:44:59.930
Thanks for taking care of him, Azaka.

00:45:09.590 --> 00:45:10.470
Yes.

00:45:10.470 --> 00:45:13.060
The incident was settled without any trouble.

00:45:13.850 --> 00:45:18.350
And I don't see Shiki around.

00:45:22.460 --> 00:45:25.590
She's pretty generous, huh?

00:45:25.590 --> 00:45:28.640
She did do her best this time, so I'm sure it's a reward.

00:45:28.640 --> 00:45:29.610
Touko?

00:45:31.110 --> 00:45:33.870
God's Word Mayday.

00:45:34.220 --> 00:45:38.120
It seems even the magus designated to be sealed wasted his efforts this time.

00:45:38.590 --> 00:45:39.890
Touko?

00:45:39.890 --> 00:45:42.710
Can you tell Azaka that she did well?

00:45:42.710 --> 00:45:45.310
Oh, okay. I'll be sure to tell her.

00:45:58.790 --> 00:46:00.770
Mikiya, where's Shiki?

00:46:00.770 --> 00:46:02.650
I think she already went home.

00:46:03.400 --> 00:46:04.930
Did you have some business with her?

00:46:06.010 --> 00:46:07.130
No.

00:46:09.670 --> 00:46:14.160
Anyway, did you hear that Tachibana regained consciousness?

00:46:15.240 --> 00:46:16.050
Yeah.

00:46:16.390 --> 00:46:20.750
According to the testimony, she unfortunately happened to be around

00:46:20.750 --> 00:46:23.320
when Hayama collapsed from a fit in October.

00:46:23.750 --> 00:46:29.000
And Hayama drugged her so she wouldn't tell everyone.

00:46:30.470 --> 00:46:32.680
She was a victim too.

00:46:33.070 --> 00:46:34.860
It's a sad memory.

00:46:35.870 --> 00:46:37.750
I hope she can forget it.

00:46:59.860 --> 00:47:01.270
Eh, wait!

00:47:02.140 --> 00:47:03.820
Azaka, what about the bus?

00:47:04.680 --> 00:47:06.340
It's cold!

00:47:10.460 --> 00:47:13.480
I'm hungry, Mikiya.

00:47:14.900 --> 00:47:17.600
Is there a place to eat around here?

00:47:18.000 --> 00:47:20.720
There's a café at the bottom of the hill.

00:47:20.720 --> 00:47:22.160
That's far.

00:47:22.160 --> 00:47:25.730
You have to make up for ignoring me and going out with Shiki the other day.

00:47:26.800 --> 00:47:28.730
If you bring that up...

00:47:28.730 --> 00:47:31.380
Then please don't complain.

00:48:03.860 --> 00:48:06.350
I had a dream about my childhood.

00:48:07.780 --> 00:48:12.580
A person who was important to my brother and me died.

00:48:14.570 --> 00:48:16.910
He looked really sad,

00:48:17.770 --> 00:48:21.410
but he didn't shed a single tear.

00:48:26.770 --> 00:48:28.650
Why won't you cry?

00:48:30.030 --> 00:48:31.570
I don't know.

00:48:32.130 --> 00:48:34.690
Is it because boys shouldn't cry?

00:48:36.740 --> 00:48:39.160
Hey, why won't you cry?

00:48:39.460 --> 00:48:41.720
I couldn't cry even if I wanted to.

00:48:42.160 --> 00:48:45.110
Because crying is a special thing.

00:48:47.300 --> 00:48:50.240
His strength touched my heart.

00:48:51.570 --> 00:48:55.720
He's normal, and he doesn't hurt others more than anyone.

00:48:55.720 --> 00:48:59.890
He can understand anyone, but nobody notices him.

00:48:59.890 --> 00:49:01.740
An empty loneliness.

00:49:04.620 --> 00:49:05.750
I think at that moment,

00:49:06.370 --> 00:49:10.550
Mikiya Kokutou became a valuable person to me.

00:49:11.110 --> 00:49:14.890
A person I can't lose no matter what.

00:49:23.050 --> 00:49:27.240
Under the starlit sky, we siblings gazed up at the starry sky.

00:49:27.950 --> 00:49:31.460
This is my primary image.

00:49:32.590 --> 00:49:37.700
It was a dream from a distant day I should never remember.

